wrote:

>
> Okay then. But then consonantal syllables are equally bad. Either it's
> Japanese CVCV intensive style or Serbian CCCC style but not somewhat
> Serbian, somewhat Japanese in different places.
>

It's somewhere in between: We could say there are 13 types of syllable: CV,
CCV and CVC from gismu, plus CVV from cmavo, plus CVVC from lujvo, plus
CCCV, CCVC, CCVV, CCCVC, CCCVV, CCVVC, CCCVVC from fu'ivla. Plus the
unlucky thirteenth: CR consonantal syllables from type-3 fu'ivla.

mu'o mi'e xorxes

